WEBVTT

00:00.200 --> 00:03.300
(Previously on...)
You didn't tell anyone I like BL, did you?

00:03.400 --> 00:04.967
No, but on one condition.

00:05.067 --> 00:07.076
You have to eat lunch with
me every day from now on.

00:07.100 --> 00:09.333
I'm counting on you for
the novel, Teacher Suzuki.

00:09.433 --> 00:10.233
Teacher?

00:10.333 --> 00:11.000
Wait a sec, Serizawa.

00:11.100 --> 00:13.276
What we just talked about is a
secret between Suzuki and me.

00:13.300 --> 00:14.700
So annoying.

00:14.800 --> 00:15.909
This makes absolutely no sense.

00:15.933 --> 00:17.700
You'll get used to Serizawa in no time.

00:17.800 --> 00:19.367
Oh, sorry.

00:19.633 --> 00:21.433
I just wanted to hear your voice.

00:21.533 --> 00:22.767
Huh?

00:22.867 --> 00:26.167
I really don't deserve
to be called a teacher.

00:26.267 --> 00:28.267
The great parts of your novel, Suzuki...

00:28.367 --> 00:29.676
And the parts that make
my heart skip a beat...

00:29.700 --> 00:31.233
Until you can see them for yourself...

00:31.333 --> 00:33.333
I'll point them all out to you.

00:33.833 --> 00:35.267
Serizawa...

00:38.267 --> 00:40.033
Suzuki.

00:41.700 --> 00:42.967
Morning.

00:43.367 --> 00:44.533
Morning.

00:44.633 --> 00:46.200
Brought your lunch today?

00:46.767 --> 00:48.000
Yeah.

00:48.667 --> 00:50.767
Your lunch box is so cute, Suzuki.

00:50.867 --> 00:54.600
It's been two weeks since I started eating
lunch with The Popular Clique's Big Four.

00:54.700 --> 00:56.133
Uh, sorry about this.

00:56.567 --> 00:58.467
I'm always crashing your lunch.

00:59.206 --> 01:01.273
No, it's totally fine.

01:01.367 --> 01:03.267
What's up man?

01:04.033 --> 01:05.600
Morning, Suzuki.

01:06.433 --> 01:08.233
Morning, Serizawa.

01:10.533 --> 01:13.200
Teacher, how's the novel coming along?

01:14.467 --> 01:16.167
I've made a little progress.

01:16.267 --> 01:17.267
That's awesome!

01:17.367 --> 01:18.700
Let me read it later.

01:20.267 --> 01:23.000
Um, I'm right here, you know.

01:23.100 --> 01:24.600
Oh, my bad, my bad.

01:24.700 --> 01:27.467
By the way, what were you just
talking about with my Suzuki?

01:27.567 --> 01:29.967
He's not your Suzuki.

01:30.367 --> 01:31.667
Morning!

01:31.767 --> 01:32.367
Alright.

01:32.467 --> 01:34.567
- Morning.
- That's way too much.

01:34.667 --> 01:37.067
Morning...

01:37.467 --> 01:41.800
Lately, my classmates have started
talking to me on their own.

01:41.900 --> 01:42.733
What?

01:42.833 --> 01:43.567
A snack party?

01:43.667 --> 01:44.433
Yeah.

01:44.533 --> 01:46.467
I heard Koharu got them from a senior.

01:46.567 --> 01:47.667
Yeah, that's right.

01:47.767 --> 01:49.600
- She said everyone can share.
- Really?

01:49.700 --> 01:51.267
- Thanks.
- Don't mention it.

01:51.367 --> 01:53.300
- So many kinds.
- Pick one.

01:53.400 --> 01:54.520
Which one should I choose...

01:54.600 --> 01:56.233
Suzuki, you'll have some too, right?

01:57.100 --> 01:58.333
But...

01:59.233 --> 02:00.633
Come on, join us.

02:01.333 --> 02:03.067
Come on, get over here.

02:04.167 --> 02:05.700
Okay, thanks.

02:05.800 --> 02:07.067
Alright!

02:07.167 --> 02:09.733
Even though there are still
many things I'm not used to,

02:09.833 --> 02:11.143
honestly, I'm having a pretty good time.

02:11.167 --> 02:11.933
I'll go with this one.

02:12.033 --> 02:12.767
Okay.

02:12.867 --> 02:13.700
Nice choice.

02:13.800 --> 02:14.967
Looks delicious.

02:18.367 --> 02:19.200
Here.

02:19.300 --> 02:20.033
Say ah!

02:20.133 --> 02:21.600
I can feed myself.

02:21.700 --> 02:22.967
What's the big deal?

02:23.067 --> 02:24.867
I want to feed you too. Here, Suzuki.

02:24.967 --> 02:25.433
Say ah!

02:25.533 --> 02:26.433
- This is fun.
- Me too...

02:26.533 --> 02:27.633
Here, say ah...

02:27.733 --> 02:29.267
- Come on.
- Here...

02:29.567 --> 02:30.300
I can feed myself!

02:30.400 --> 02:31.467
- Ah...
- Come on.

02:31.567 --> 02:32.333
- Me too...
- Got some right here.

02:32.433 --> 02:33.300
You guys.

02:33.400 --> 02:34.633
Come on...

02:34.733 --> 02:37.367
Are you treating Suzuki
like a deer in Nara?

02:39.400 --> 02:41.000
What, is an alien speaking?

02:41.833 --> 02:42.833
Hey!

02:42.900 --> 02:44.500
I'm the one speaking.

02:44.900 --> 02:45.533
Seems like it.

02:45.633 --> 02:46.700
Oh, thanks.

02:46.800 --> 02:47.833
What are you guys doing?

02:47.933 --> 02:49.233
We're going to be late.

02:49.867 --> 02:50.867
Huh?

02:50.933 --> 02:51.600
I'll take this then.

02:51.700 --> 02:53.367
Yeah, here.

02:53.667 --> 02:54.567
Here.

02:54.667 --> 02:55.300
This is the biggest piece.

02:55.400 --> 02:56.400
Ah...

02:56.500 --> 02:58.733
Hey, um... is that...?

03:07.333 --> 03:08.700
Yuma, this is really good.

03:08.800 --> 03:11.200
- Really?
- Yeah, here, say ah!

03:12.667 --> 03:15.000
By the way, "Suzubi"...

03:15.100 --> 03:16.200
Suzubi?

03:16.300 --> 03:18.933
When did you get so close
to Serizawa and the guys?

03:19.033 --> 03:21.133
- Huh?
- I've actually been a bit curious.

03:21.233 --> 03:22.709
You guys just suddenly got super tight.

03:22.733 --> 03:24.000
Yeah.

03:38.867 --> 03:42.367
Can I really consider them my friends?

03:51.467 --> 03:52.500
Pass it to me!

03:52.700 --> 03:53.700
Here.

03:54.400 --> 03:55.633
- Huh?
- Takeuchi.

03:55.733 --> 03:57.300
It wasn't me, it wasn't me!

03:57.400 --> 03:59.533
- It wasn't me, it wasn't me!
- You totally did that.

04:00.633 --> 04:03.067
How dare you mess with me!

04:04.600 --> 04:08.500
To call us friends, we live in
completely different worlds.

04:50.967 --> 04:54.000
"Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me"

04:55.967 --> 04:58.700
(Episode 3)

04:58.800 --> 05:02.067
At the end of the day,
what even defines a friend?

05:04.867 --> 05:07.933
(Friend Standard)

05:11.300 --> 05:14.980
"What defines a friend? What do you guys think?
1. Accepts the real you 2. Fun to be around."

05:16.100 --> 05:18.300
The real me...

05:20.667 --> 05:24.367
By the way, what's the deal with Suzuki?

05:24.467 --> 05:25.067
Right?

05:25.167 --> 05:27.043
How did he suddenly get so tight
with The Popular Clique's Big Four?

05:27.067 --> 05:30.367
It makes absolutely no sense. They're
in a totally different league than Suzuki.

05:43.533 --> 05:44.800
Suzuki!

05:45.533 --> 05:47.133
Finally found you.

05:48.000 --> 05:49.000
Serizawa.

05:49.100 --> 05:50.667
So this is where you've been.

05:50.767 --> 05:52.533
I've been looking all over for you.

05:53.400 --> 05:55.200
Wh-What's wrong?

05:55.500 --> 05:56.200
Nothing.

05:56.300 --> 05:58.233
You just left without saying a word.

05:58.333 --> 05:59.600
I felt so lonely.

06:00.967 --> 06:01.867
Sorry.

06:01.967 --> 06:03.933
You guys were having
such a great time chatting,

06:04.033 --> 06:05.633
I felt a bit awkward interrupting.

06:07.033 --> 06:09.867
Next time, at least say a
proper goodbye to me.

06:10.900 --> 06:11.900
Yeah.

06:11.967 --> 06:13.800
By the way, are you free today?

06:14.367 --> 06:15.367
Uh...

06:16.533 --> 06:17.200
Yeah.

06:17.300 --> 06:19.409
Then do you want to go sing karaoke
with everyone right now?

06:19.433 --> 06:20.133
With everyone?

06:20.233 --> 06:22.333
- Yeah.
- Karaoke?

06:22.433 --> 06:23.800
Here, this way.

06:31.133 --> 06:32.000
Hey.

06:32.100 --> 06:33.400
Let's go, let's go.

06:33.500 --> 06:34.767
Suzuki.

06:36.267 --> 06:37.267
Hey.

06:41.833 --> 06:43.967
Matsuno, what's wrong?

06:45.433 --> 06:47.233
Oh, nothing...

06:47.333 --> 06:49.333
Never mind, sorry.

06:50.467 --> 06:52.600
Wh-What should I do?

06:52.700 --> 06:55.833
I had a moment of weakness
and just tagged along.

06:55.933 --> 07:01.067
But in front of The Popular Clique's Big
Four, I don't even know a single hype song.

07:01.167 --> 07:02.167
Cheers!

07:02.267 --> 07:04.167
I want to sing Chicken.

07:04.267 --> 07:05.700
What's that?

07:06.533 --> 07:08.600
Bump of Chicken, obviously!

07:08.700 --> 07:09.367
"Bump of Chicken"?

07:09.467 --> 07:11.900
- And "Higedan".
- Your abbreviations are way too weird.

07:12.000 --> 07:13.767
- Higedan?
- Official Hige Dandism!

07:13.867 --> 07:14.600
- What?
- Hige?

07:14.700 --> 07:17.167
- Are you out of your mind?
- Hey...

07:17.267 --> 07:18.167
Here you go, Suzuki.

07:18.267 --> 07:20.100
Oh, thanks.

07:22.333 --> 07:24.333
What do you usually sing, Suzuki?

07:26.500 --> 07:28.567
Uh, well...

07:29.500 --> 07:30.767
What's wrong?

07:32.800 --> 07:35.333
Actually, well...

07:36.367 --> 07:39.167
I'm not really used to karaoke.

07:39.700 --> 07:44.567
And I don't think I've ever
sung in front of people before.

07:44.667 --> 07:46.567
Seriously? My bad.

07:46.667 --> 07:50.067
I'm not really familiar
with recent songs either.

07:54.767 --> 07:57.067
Then I'll help you look for one.

07:58.400 --> 07:59.400
Huh?

08:00.300 --> 08:02.400
Here, hand it over.

08:04.900 --> 08:06.633
First, press here.

08:07.400 --> 08:08.800
Okay.

08:08.900 --> 08:10.167
Then press here.

08:10.267 --> 08:11.267
Okay.

08:12.000 --> 08:13.300
And then do this.

08:13.400 --> 08:17.400
Oh, I can do it myself.

08:18.367 --> 08:19.433
It's fine.

08:19.533 --> 08:22.567
Come on, let's start from the "A" section.

08:23.367 --> 08:25.500
Tell me if you recognize any songs.

08:27.300 --> 08:27.867
Time to dig in!

08:27.967 --> 08:29.233
Hey...

08:29.333 --> 08:30.033
You're eating way too much.

08:30.133 --> 08:30.633
What's the big deal?

08:30.733 --> 08:32.767
(Song Title: Hometown)
There's plenty left anyway.

08:32.867 --> 08:33.967
Huh?

08:34.433 --> 08:35.467
Oh.

08:35.567 --> 08:37.333
It's finally Suzuki's turn.

08:37.433 --> 08:39.400
That's a really weird song choice.

08:39.500 --> 08:40.933
I'm so nervous.

08:41.033 --> 08:42.143
- You got this, Suzuki!
- Awesome, awesome!

08:42.167 --> 08:43.433
Stand up and sing...

08:48.500 --> 08:51.700
(Fishing for minnows in that river)

08:53.967 --> 08:55.467
Sorry, I really can't do this.

08:56.233 --> 08:57.633
Suzuki, are you okay?

08:57.733 --> 08:58.876
You don't have to force
yourself if you don't want to sing.

08:58.900 --> 08:59.333
Yeah.

08:59.433 --> 09:01.900
Here, want some fries?

09:02.300 --> 09:04.500
Here, have some more fries.

09:04.600 --> 09:05.733
Um.

09:05.833 --> 09:07.433
I'm going to grab a drink.

09:08.233 --> 09:09.933
Do you guys want anything?

09:10.667 --> 09:12.933
I'll take a melon soda.

09:13.033 --> 09:13.667
Melon soda it is.

09:13.767 --> 09:15.900
- Melon soda?
- Yep, melon soda.

09:16.000 --> 09:17.080
Can I get an iced tea then?

09:17.167 --> 09:18.000
Sure.

09:18.100 --> 09:19.740
- Could you grab me one too?
- You got it.

09:21.100 --> 09:22.333
Here, it's all yours.

09:24.733 --> 09:25.367
Huh?

09:25.467 --> 09:26.533
What are you doing?

09:26.633 --> 09:27.433
Then I'll go with you.

09:27.533 --> 09:29.200
Hold on a sec.

09:29.300 --> 09:30.533
You're up next.

09:30.633 --> 09:33.067
- Come on, sit down.
- Pick a song.

09:33.167 --> 09:34.676
- I'm gonna go get some drinks.
- Sorry about that.

09:34.700 --> 09:36.109
- In that case...
- Aren't you gonna sing?

09:36.133 --> 09:37.167
- Hype it up!
- Okay.

09:37.433 --> 09:38.900
- Get the crowd going!
- Okay.

09:39.000 --> 09:40.333
I'll sing backup then.

09:40.433 --> 09:40.967
You good?

09:41.067 --> 09:42.700
- Can you do it?
- Let me think.

09:43.733 --> 09:47.433
(Melon Soda)

09:48.233 --> 09:50.300
You guys actually invited me out.

09:52.100 --> 09:53.967
I guess this is still too hard for me.

09:54.067 --> 09:55.176
You can sing for everyone next time.

09:55.200 --> 09:56.400
- Why? You have to sing!
- No.

09:56.500 --> 09:59.067
Nakamura's been hogging the mic anyway.

10:00.967 --> 10:02.633
Huh? Suzuki?

10:05.100 --> 10:07.833
Wow, it really is Suzuki.

10:08.300 --> 10:09.667
Long time no see.

10:11.233 --> 10:13.000
Um...

10:13.867 --> 10:15.200
Long time no see...

10:16.200 --> 10:20.733
You're... not alone.

10:22.700 --> 10:23.700
Yeah...

10:24.433 --> 10:26.833
I'm here with some classmates.

10:26.933 --> 10:27.833
Huh?

10:27.933 --> 10:30.800
Are you with Serizawa and his crew?

10:30.900 --> 10:33.033
Yeah, pretty much.

10:33.133 --> 10:35.467
No way.

10:35.567 --> 10:38.067
I noticed something.

10:38.167 --> 10:42.000
Why have you been hanging out with
The Popular Clique's Big Four lately?

10:42.100 --> 10:44.567
Oh, no, it just kind of happened.

10:44.667 --> 10:47.100
I can't believe you're
hanging with the A-listers.

10:49.133 --> 10:53.200
You're completely different
from them, aren't you?

10:53.300 --> 10:54.567
That's insane.

10:54.667 --> 10:58.200
But aren't Serizawa and his crew
just messing with you?

10:58.300 --> 10:59.633
That sucks.

11:00.500 --> 11:02.400
Hey, are you okay?

11:02.500 --> 11:03.943
Are they treating you like an errand boy?

11:03.967 --> 11:05.800
Ah, probably.

11:05.900 --> 11:07.467
That's definitely it.

11:07.567 --> 11:08.967
No, they're not like that...

11:09.067 --> 11:10.267
By the way, Suzuki.

11:11.133 --> 11:13.067
Are you still reading BL?

11:18.500 --> 11:19.609
Look, you made him freeze up.

11:19.633 --> 11:21.733
I didn't mean to, I didn't mean to.

11:21.833 --> 11:23.167
Hey.

11:25.000 --> 11:26.633
What's wrong with that?

11:34.433 --> 11:37.133
I love BL too.

11:38.900 --> 11:40.567
What's so weird about it?

11:42.333 --> 11:45.033
Serizawa...

11:47.033 --> 11:48.600
You guys are so pathetic.

11:49.667 --> 11:51.633
Just because you don't understand it,

11:52.300 --> 11:55.367
don't trash what other people care about!

11:55.467 --> 11:59.200
No... I didn't mean it like that...

11:59.600 --> 12:01.000
What's going on?

12:01.100 --> 12:02.567
Are you guys fighting?

12:02.667 --> 12:04.833
I thought I heard you talking about BL.

12:04.933 --> 12:06.100
Uh, well...

12:06.200 --> 12:08.433
More importantly, who are you guys?

12:09.167 --> 12:16.167
Uh... they were my
friends in freshman year.

12:18.867 --> 12:20.667
People who used to be my friends...

12:26.467 --> 12:31.000
I don't know if you're
ex-friends or what,

12:31.100 --> 12:36.000
but could you stop bothering our Suzuki?

12:37.367 --> 12:38.800
Sure thing.

12:39.267 --> 12:40.433
- Let's go.
- Okay...

12:40.767 --> 12:42.700
Matsuno... hurry up.

12:49.433 --> 12:50.667
Are you okay?

12:50.767 --> 12:51.833
Yeah.

12:51.933 --> 12:53.233
Thanks.

12:57.100 --> 12:58.667
What happened?

13:11.433 --> 13:14.000
Back in middle school,

13:14.100 --> 13:17.167
I was really stressed out
about exams for a while.

13:18.267 --> 13:21.867
I wanted a change of pace,

13:21.967 --> 13:24.867
and a BL drama popped
up in my recommendations.

13:24.967 --> 13:27.500
I just clicked on it on a whim.

13:30.733 --> 13:32.200
I'm here!

13:33.367 --> 13:34.533
Huh?

13:34.633 --> 13:35.633
Why?

13:41.433 --> 13:43.200
Didn't I say I'd come?

13:48.733 --> 13:51.167
Since it was a high school drama,

13:51.267 --> 13:54.800
at first, I just admired it,
wishing I could have

13:54.900 --> 13:58.433
such a sparkling
high school life too.

13:59.200 --> 14:00.667
Why?

14:01.800 --> 14:05.467
I can't take it anymore.

14:05.567 --> 14:07.300
I'm so tired.

14:16.000 --> 14:17.467
Me too.

14:29.467 --> 14:32.533
Before I knew it, I was completely hooked.

14:33.100 --> 14:34.620
The more I watched, the deeper I fell.

14:35.767 --> 14:38.467
Then I started reading
novels and manga too.

14:40.567 --> 14:42.633
And every single one was amazing.

14:43.933 --> 14:46.233
They were all such gentle worlds.

14:48.700 --> 14:50.633
Only during those moments...

14:50.733 --> 14:53.700
could I forget everything I hated.

14:55.667 --> 14:59.500
But during my freshman year,

15:00.533 --> 15:02.600
I accidentally brought it up with them,

15:02.700 --> 15:04.300
and they totally judged me for it.

15:08.833 --> 15:10.533
I seriously didn't sleep at all.

15:10.633 --> 15:12.400
Go to sleep then.

15:12.500 --> 15:15.133
I have an event tomorrow, so I
have to pull another all-nighter.

15:15.233 --> 15:17.343
- You're way too obsessed with mobile games.
- Give it a rest.

15:17.367 --> 15:18.200
What about you, Suzuki?

15:18.300 --> 15:20.833
I've been really into BL lately.

15:20.933 --> 15:22.000
Huh?

15:22.100 --> 15:23.167
BL?

15:23.267 --> 15:24.609
Like, guys falling in love with guys?

15:24.633 --> 15:26.867
Yeah, it's really good.
It's just a love story.

15:26.967 --> 15:28.333
And it makes your heart flutter.

15:28.433 --> 15:30.209
It makes you feel like you
can truly fall for someone.

15:30.233 --> 15:31.933
It's really nice.

15:34.400 --> 15:38.100
Wait, Suzuki, are you one of those?

15:39.100 --> 15:40.500
Huh? One of what?

15:40.600 --> 15:41.867
You know...

15:43.267 --> 15:44.267
Ah...

15:50.167 --> 15:53.967
Are you and Matsuno in
that kind of relationship?

15:54.067 --> 15:56.600
What are you talking about?

15:56.700 --> 15:57.433
Of course not.

15:57.533 --> 16:00.000
- That's gross.
- Hey, knock it off.

16:00.100 --> 16:02.333
- You guys make a cute couple.
- No, we don't.

16:02.433 --> 16:03.443
- Stop it.
- Give him a hug!

16:03.467 --> 16:05.476
- Are you a top or a bottom?
- Don't get the wrong idea.

16:05.500 --> 16:06.709
- What top or bottom?
- Which one is it?

16:06.733 --> 16:07.300
Aren't you gay?

16:07.400 --> 16:08.400
That's not true at all.

16:08.567 --> 16:09.067
Seriously.

16:09.167 --> 16:11.533
- You're lying, right?
- Yeah, totally.

16:16.533 --> 16:20.367
Since then, I kept it a
secret from everyone.

16:20.800 --> 16:22.933
I just enjoyed it by myself.

16:29.533 --> 16:33.433
Ah... sorry for bringing
this up out of nowhere.

16:34.333 --> 16:35.900
It's fine.

16:36.367 --> 16:38.367
If you like BL,

16:38.467 --> 16:40.043
doesn't that make you just like Serizawa?

16:40.067 --> 16:43.167
Oh, is that how you guys got close?

16:43.267 --> 16:44.500
Yeah.

16:44.600 --> 16:48.667
Actually, I write novels based on Serizawa.

16:48.767 --> 16:49.633
What!?

16:49.733 --> 16:51.200
Suzuki, you write novels too?

16:51.300 --> 16:52.000
That's awesome.

16:52.100 --> 16:54.200
I want to read your novels too, Suzuki.

16:55.067 --> 16:57.200
Plus, I like BL as well.

16:57.300 --> 16:58.309
You like it too, Takeuchi?

16:58.333 --> 17:01.500
To be honest, I've been
reading it longer than Serizawa.

17:01.600 --> 17:03.133
We've read it too.

17:03.233 --> 17:05.733
Yeah, Serizawa kept forcing it on us.

17:05.833 --> 17:07.900
I've read manga.

17:08.000 --> 17:09.533
It's actually pretty good.

17:09.626 --> 17:10.626
He only reads manga.

17:10.733 --> 17:12.333
Yeah.

17:17.100 --> 17:18.300
What's wrong?

17:18.400 --> 17:19.900
Suzuki.

17:20.500 --> 17:23.367
Nothing, I just feel like...

17:24.667 --> 17:26.867
this world is so gentle.

17:31.467 --> 17:33.700
See, what did I tell you?

17:33.800 --> 17:37.100
They don't care about stuff like that.

17:40.433 --> 17:45.267
But out of everyone in the world, I'm
the one who wants to treat Suzuki the best.

17:51.733 --> 17:53.733
What's gotten into you?

17:54.267 --> 17:56.300
I think I can sing now.

17:56.400 --> 17:57.633
Wait... now!?

17:58.200 --> 17:59.967
That's the spirit, Suzuki!

18:00.067 --> 18:01.067
Come on, sing it.

18:01.133 --> 18:01.467
Okay.

18:01.567 --> 18:03.067
Go for it, Suzuki!

18:03.167 --> 18:04.500
Nice, let's go.

18:09.333 --> 18:11.100
Get ready.

18:12.200 --> 18:13.333
Show 'em what you got.

18:14.467 --> 18:15.000
Here we go.

18:15.467 --> 18:21.433
♪ Chasing rabbits on that mountain ♪

18:21.533 --> 18:24.367
♪ Hey! ♪

18:24.467 --> 18:31.167
♪ Catching minnows in that stream ♪

18:31.667 --> 18:33.033
♪ Hey! ♪

18:33.133 --> 18:35.500
- ♪ Still swirling in my dreams ♪
- Don't worry about it.

18:35.600 --> 18:36.300
Keep it up, Suzuki!

18:36.400 --> 18:40.267
♪ Unforgettable is my hometown ♪

18:45.533 --> 18:47.667
Oh crap, run!

18:47.767 --> 18:48.367
Here.

18:48.467 --> 18:49.467
Here.

18:51.000 --> 18:51.600
Give it back.

18:51.700 --> 18:52.167
Here you go.

18:52.267 --> 18:53.267
Okay.

18:53.433 --> 18:54.667
We're doomed.

18:54.767 --> 18:59.467
So, how did it feel? Singing in
front of people for the first time?

18:59.733 --> 19:02.133
Ah, well...

19:02.767 --> 19:04.800
It wasn't quite what I expected.

19:05.667 --> 19:08.200
It felt like no one was
really listening to me sing.

19:08.300 --> 19:09.367
- Hey!
- Hey!

19:09.467 --> 19:13.200
Yeah... that's pretty much how it goes.

19:13.833 --> 19:15.409
But thanks to that, I realized something.

19:15.433 --> 19:16.767
Huh?

19:16.967 --> 19:21.633
You don't really need to care
so much about what others think.

19:22.167 --> 19:25.867
The things you cherish,

19:25.967 --> 19:28.567
just enjoy your own world to the fullest.

19:30.433 --> 19:33.267
Yeah, you're right.

19:35.400 --> 19:37.200
Thank you, Serizawa.

19:38.133 --> 19:39.967
Thanks for inviting me today.

19:42.833 --> 19:45.800
And thanks for standing up for me.

19:47.300 --> 19:49.067
It was nothing.

19:49.300 --> 19:52.833
Oh, Suzuki, do you still have some time?

19:53.167 --> 19:54.467
Huh?

20:01.067 --> 20:03.833
(Banana Lake)

20:03.933 --> 20:06.033
Looks so good...

20:09.667 --> 20:12.533
We come here all the time.

20:13.133 --> 20:16.200
The fries here are amazing.

20:16.300 --> 20:19.367
Especially with the
truffle mayo, it's the best.

20:19.467 --> 20:22.167
I recommend the pesto pasta.

20:22.267 --> 20:24.533
No... you gotta try the
fried chicken and pudding.

20:25.433 --> 20:26.667
Pudding...

20:26.767 --> 20:28.067
Which one are you craving?

20:28.167 --> 20:29.967
Suzuki, what do you want to eat first?

20:30.067 --> 20:31.100
Come on.

20:31.200 --> 20:33.633
- This one is the best.
- No, this one is better.

20:34.033 --> 20:34.467
Pesto...

20:34.567 --> 20:35.367
Fries!

20:35.467 --> 20:36.900
- Pudding...
- Pesto pasta.

20:37.000 --> 20:38.067
Hmm?

20:39.000 --> 20:41.800
Are you actually not hungry?

20:44.633 --> 20:46.100
I see...

20:46.200 --> 20:47.767
Well, nothing we can do about that.

20:49.433 --> 20:50.433
No...

20:51.100 --> 20:52.433
It's not that.

20:52.933 --> 20:54.100
Yeah.

20:54.200 --> 20:57.667
I'm just feeling the fun.

20:59.300 --> 21:01.733
And I...

21:04.300 --> 21:06.733
I'm just so happy right now.

21:13.133 --> 21:14.733
So cute.

21:16.367 --> 21:17.367
Cute?

21:17.400 --> 21:18.200
Me?

21:18.300 --> 21:20.233
Who else would I be talking about?

21:20.333 --> 21:22.667
You're seriously way too cute.

21:23.100 --> 21:25.700
Here, just eat something first.

21:25.800 --> 21:27.533
Say ah.

21:28.633 --> 21:29.533
Oh?

21:29.633 --> 21:30.267
He ate it!

21:30.367 --> 21:31.467
Hey, that's not fair!

21:31.567 --> 21:32.576
Suzuki, eat this too. Have mine.

21:32.600 --> 21:33.500
Say ah.

21:33.600 --> 21:36.200
I've got some too, with mayo on it.

21:36.300 --> 21:36.900
Come on.

21:37.000 --> 21:39.833
Hey, you guys, stop feeding
my Suzuki without permission.

21:39.933 --> 21:40.467
Ah.

21:40.567 --> 21:42.233
You've got some nerve saying "feeding."

21:42.333 --> 21:43.609
And he's not "your" Suzuki, okay?

21:43.633 --> 21:44.733
Exactly.

21:44.833 --> 21:45.733
Suzuki belongs to everyone.

21:45.833 --> 21:46.533
Yeah.

21:46.633 --> 21:48.143
- What the heck?
- Suzuki belongs to us.

21:48.167 --> 21:49.000
What, you wanna fight?

21:49.100 --> 21:50.443
Bring it on! I'll take you all on.

21:50.467 --> 21:51.633
Here I come.

21:51.733 --> 21:54.300
Alright, I'm fully charged.

21:54.400 --> 21:55.533
Okay...

21:55.633 --> 21:56.976
- It's too late to back out now.
- Wait...

21:57.000 --> 21:58.367
Wait, stop fighting!

21:59.067 --> 22:00.667
We're just kidding.

22:00.767 --> 22:02.143
- Sorry about that.
- Thank goodness.

22:02.167 --> 22:03.167
- Pow!
- Ouch!

22:03.233 --> 22:04.393
What are you saying ouch for?

22:05.567 --> 22:09.633
Anyway, I'm number one in Suzuki's heart.

22:11.200 --> 22:12.467
Right?

22:19.133 --> 22:20.033
Let's eat before it gets cold.

22:20.133 --> 22:21.267
Come on.

22:22.767 --> 22:23.767
Let's eat.

22:34.233 --> 22:35.267
It's really good.

22:44.367 --> 22:47.267
(Next Episode Preview)
Suzuki, do you like Serizawa?

22:47.367 --> 22:47.867
Huh?

22:47.967 --> 22:49.167
I told you it's not like that.

22:49.533 --> 22:50.600
I really want to see you.

22:50.700 --> 22:52.300
I can feed myself.

22:52.400 --> 22:54.367
- I should probably head back...
- Don't go.

22:54.467 --> 22:55.767
Stay with me until morning.

22:56.333 --> 22:59.000
(This drama is purely fictional)
Is this how friends act?
